# Weekly Paid Media Report — 2026-10-24 to 2026-10-30

Data complete through **2026-10-30** (account anchor date). All figures are platform-reported
(spend, conversions, CPA from google_ads / meta_ads / reddit_ads via platform checks and
week-over-week comparisons). Comparisons are last week (2026-10-24 → 10-30) vs prior week
(2026-10-17 → 10-23).

---

## Account summary

| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $9,892.11 | $11,844.59 | +$1,952.48 (+19.7%) |
| Conversions | 53 | 65 | +12 (+22.6%) |
| Blended CPA (derived) | $186.64 | $182.22 | −$4.42 (−2.4%) |

Efficiency held while volume scaled: spend and conversions grew together, and blended CPA
improved slightly.

## Per-platform detail

### Google Ads — search product terms / brand awareness
| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $5,377.43 | $8,029.35 | +$2,651.92 (+49.3%) |
| Conversions | 28 | 42 | +14 (+50.0%) |
| CPA | $192.05 | $191.18 | −$0.87 (−0.5%) |

Most likely driver: the July decision to shift ~15% of search budget toward brand awareness
added delivery, and conversions scaled in line with spend — CPA was unaffected.

### Meta Ads — retargeting
| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $3,761.84 | $3,039.99 | −$721.85 (−19.2%) |
| Conversions | 19 | 16 | −3 (−15.8%) |
| CPA | $197.99 | $190.00 | −$7.99 (−4.0%) |

Most likely driver: spend was reduced and conversions fell almost proportionally
(−19.2% vs −15.8%), so this reads as deliberate throttling, not audience fatigue —
efficiency actually improved.

### Reddit Ads — community boost (long-run experiment)
| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $752.84 | $775.25 | +$22.41 (+3.0%) |
| Conversions | 6 | 7 | +1 (+16.7%) |
| CPA | $125.47 | $110.75 | −$14.72 (−11.7%) |

Most likely driver: flat spend with one extra conversion is what improved CPA; at 7
conversions/week this is directionally good, not statistically settled.

## Recommendations — one per platform

1. **Google Ads** — Scale: raise budget ~10% ($8,029 → ~$8,832/wk). The account absorbed
   +49.3% spend with CPA flat (−0.5%), and search product terms is the protected top
   pipeline driver. Guardrail: revert if CPA exceeds $200 for 3 consecutive days.
   → Proposal **prop-846b8fb4** (pending approval).
2. **Meta Ads** — No budget change. Spend was cut −19.2% and efficiency improved (CPA
   −4.0%); the drop in conversions (19 → 16) tracks the spend reduction. Watch one more
   week before drawing conclusions.
3. **Reddit Ads** — Scale modestly: +20% budget ($775 → ~$930/wk) as a low-risk test of
   the account's best CPA ($110.75). Small volume; review after 2 weeks.
   → Proposal **prop-c0b3b28e** (pending approval).

## Caveats

- **Conversions are platform-reported.** Conversion definitions differ per platform and are
  not comparable as outcomes; they are not qualified leads. Pipeline/lead outcomes are
  warehouse-sourced and were not pulled for this report.
- **Reddit volume is small** (6–7 conversions/wk): percentage moves there are noisy;
  treat the −11.7% CPA improvement as directional.
- **Recommendations 1 and 3 are proposals only** (prop-846b8fb4, prop-c0b3b28e), pending
  human approval. Nothing has been applied.
- **Keyword queue housekeeping:** three pending Google Ads keyword proposals
  (prop-110b0388, prop-7bc17e46, prop-ce20bd8e) duplicate a keyword set already applied on
  2026-11-01 (prop-b1e2ede4: "paid media analytics" phrase, "ppc attribution" phrase,
  "gtm tracking" exact). Reviewer should reject the duplicates to avoid adding the same
  keywords twice.
- Per the July decisions log, the search → brand awareness budget shift is intentional;
  any rebalancing should be discussed, not "fixed" unilaterally.

